From bfb758082ee66fd899b1c69148fb6a5171456d13 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Harshit Gupta <39994376+arelyx@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 12:58:04 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] freedreno/xenos: gl_PointCoord

- Xenos generates sprite coordinates only when the vertex shader exports
  the point size (POSITION_2_VECTORS_SPRITE): have st always add
  gl_PointSize (PIPE_POINT_SIZE_LOWER_ALWAYS).
- st then stores gl_PointSize twice (1.0, then the clamped glPointSize);
  ir2 put both into one export instruction and the hardware kept the
  first. Drop store_outputs that a later store overwrites.
- The generated parameter's sign bits flag the primitive type: abs().
- Its y grows towards GL's +y: flip it to the upper-left origin and let
  st's pntc y transform (lower_wpos_pntc) handle sprite origin and FBO
  vs window.

